rrogate half-formed ideas, research unfamiliar territory, make unlikely connections, argue with myself, edit, revise, and keep following a thought after I might otherwise have dropped it.",{"className":"$undefined","children":["I use it to think out loud, interrogate half-formed ideas, research unfamiliar territory, make unlikely connections, argue with myself, edit, revise, and keep following a thought after I might otherwise have dropped it."]}],["$","p","2-It sometimes contributes words. It often contributes questions. I discard a lot. I rewrite a lot. The work that remains is here because I recognize myself in it and am willing to put my name on it.",{"className":"$undefined","children":["It sometimes contributes words. It often contributes questions. I discard a lot. I rewrite a lot. The work that remains is here because I recognize myself in it and am willing to put my name on it."]}],["$","p","3-Working this way has made me less interested in whether something was *made with AI* than in what kind of attention went into making it. A tool can participate deeply in the process without replacing the person responsible for the choices.",{"className":"$undefined","children":["Working this way has made me less interested in whether something was ",["$","em","1",{"children":["made with AI"]}]," than in what kind of attention went into making it. A tool can participate deeply in the process without replacing the person responsible for the choices."]}],["$","p","4-For me, AI has become a way of making thinking visible. The conversation forces ideas out of their comfortable vagueness and into language, where I can finally see what I believe, what I don’t, and what deserves another pass.",{"className":"$undefined","children":["For me, AI has become a way of making thinking visible. The conversation forces ideas out of their comfortable vagueness and into language, where I can finally see what I believe, what I don’t, and what deserves another pass."]}],["$","p","5-I was 